WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.485
This chapter asks a specific question: ASI-scale systems cross organizations, jurisdictions,

2
00:00:06.485 --> 00:00:09.990
borders, public services, and affected populations.

3
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:15.414
Technical permissions and private governance cannot determine who has public authority,

4
00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:19.112
whose participation counts, how conflicting rules are resolved,

5
00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:22.810
or how international commitments are verified and amended.

6
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:28.581
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: A compliance checklist, technical standard,

7
00:00:28.581 --> 00:00:34.556
treaty text, risk framework, or corporate safety policy can name duties

8
00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:40.530
without establishing jurisdiction, representative input, assessor independence, enforcement, remedy, capacity, legitimacy,

9
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:46.175
or observed effectiveness. Architecture cannot manufacture democratic consent.

10
00:00:46.775 --> 00:00:52.583
The chapter's core claim is this: Public deployment and cross-border coordination

11
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:58.391
should proceed only through a versioned institutional packet that keeps jurisdiction,

12
00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:04.199
mandate, participation, scientific evidence, law and standards, verification, enforcement, remedy, capacity,

13
00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.255
conflict, expiry,

14
00:01:05.595 --> 00:01:11.647
and legitimacy residuals distinct; legal text, technical conformance, stakeholder consultation,

15
00:01:11.647 --> 00:01:18.304
or an international commitment alone establishes neither lawful authority, effective governance,

16
00:01:18.304 --> 00:01:20.725
representative legitimacy, nor safety.

17
00:01:21.065 --> 00:01:25.810
Map jurisdiction, mandate, standing, affected publics, representation, excluded groups,

18
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.555
and conflicts before treating an institution as an authority.

19
00:01:30.555 --> 00:01:36.354
Join public reasons and scientific evidence to a versioned law-policy-standard crosswalk

20
00:01:36.354 --> 00:01:40.045
without collapsing these different sources of legitimacy.

21
00:01:40.645 --> 00:01:44.675
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

22
00:01:45.015 --> 00:01:51.664
Build a jurisdiction-and-commitment packet and test it on public-record cases and

23
00:01:51.664 --> 00:01:58.314
adversarial multi-jurisdiction tabletop exercises containing conflicting rules, missing participation, assessor conflicts,

24
00:01:58.314 --> 00:02:02.545
evidence revision, incidents, noncompliance, and remedy requests.

25
00:02:02.885 --> 00:02:07.361
The exercise can test record completeness and conflict routing,

26
00:02:07.361 --> 00:02:11.339
not legal compliance, public trust, or geopolitical stability.

27
00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:16.809
Join public reasons and scientific evidence to a versioned law-policy-standard crosswalk

28
00:02:16.809 --> 00:02:20.290
without collapsing these different sources of legitimacy.

29
00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:27.427
Define cross-border commitments with named verification, assessor independence, noncompliance handling, enforcement,

30
00:02:27.427 --> 00:02:31.135
dispute, remedy, amendment, and withdrawal paths.

31
00:02:31.475 --> 00:02:37.795
Track institutional capacity, distributional effects, emergency authority, exceptions, capture indicators,

32
00:02:37.795 --> 00:02:40.955
and unresolved conflicts through deployment.

33
00:02:41.555 --> 00:02:46.825
The design can still fail. regulatory capture forum shopping race-to-the-bottom deployment

34
00:02:46.825 --> 00:02:52.094
standards laundering The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate,

35
00:02:52.094 --> 00:02:56.885
or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

36
00:02:57.485 --> 00:03:02.531
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

37
00:03:02.531 --> 00:03:06.660
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

38
00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.706
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

39
00:03:11.706 --> 00:03:12.165
closed.

40
00:03:12.505 --> 00:03:18.041
A finite Institutions, International Coordination, and Public Legitimacy record may hand

41
00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:22.067
off only when identity, authority, version, required checks,

42
00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:27.603
and residual ownership are present; no theorem grants empirical effectiveness or

43
00:03:27.603 --> 00:03:28.610
release authority.

44
00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:34.048
Affected and excluded populations remain visible in the denominator.

45
00:03:34.048 --> 00:03:38.580
Every commitment names verification, noncompliance, enforcement, and remedy.

46
00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:44.144
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

47
00:03:44.144 --> 00:03:49.108
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

48
00:03:49.108 --> 00:03:54.072
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

49
00:03:54.072 --> 00:03:58.585
enforcement. No safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI, or ASI conclusion follows.

50
00:03:58.925 --> 00:04:03.400
These boundaries matter because an explanatory derivative is useful only if

51
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.655
it preserves the evidence ceiling of its source.

52
00:04:07.255 --> 00:04:12.540
At most, this visual explains the chapter's design rationale at argument

53
00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.345
support; it adds no empirical, deployment, safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI,

54
00:04:17.345 --> 00:04:22.630
or ASI result. The next chapter is Societal Resilience and Misuse

55
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.110
Defense.

56
00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:29.160
It takes responsibility for Model safeguards and internal incident command cannot

57
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:34.870
by themselves protect people, institutions, and critical services when prevention fails,

58
00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:40.580
misuse diffuses across platforms, or harms exploit social and infrastructural vulnerabilities.
